--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The darkness folds back like cloth. Three cards hover before you, edges glowing.  

First turns **The High Priestess**, moon-crowned, scroll half-hidden. A hush slips through you, the same hush that lives inside library cloisters at dusk—quiet, certain, waiting.  

Second flips: **Six of Cups**, two children trading chipped clay mugs of water on a sun-dusted Aurelion street. Warmth pools behind your ribs, memory without a name.  

Third lands: **Eight of Pentacles**, a lone carpenter in Tharros counting hammer strikes. Your palms tingle, ready for work you haven’t yet chosen.  

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.  

The void peels away like wet parchment. Cold stone, pine torch-smoke, and distant harbor bells pull you upright. You are lying on the flagstones of an abandoned customs house in Virell; moonlight drips through the broken roof and sketches the card images across the floor.

